      "link": "https://fajieyuan.github.io/papers/nextitnet6.pdf",
      "contributions": [
        "Introduces causal dilated convolutions and residual blocks for sequential recommendation.",
        "Provides the architectural basis for reasoning about accessible history spans."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not establish that prefix truncation improves this benchmark.",
        "The supplied baseline's actual convolutions must be checked before calculating its receptive field."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[2] Does It Look Sequential?",
      "link": "https://github.com/Antondfger/Does-It-Look-Sequential/",
      "contributions": [
        "Motivates sequence-shuffling controls and examination of ranking quality and recommendation overlap."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Perturbation sensitivity alone establishes neither useful personalization nor current intent.",
        "Does not validate the proposed augmentation on the four supplied categories."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[3] On Sampled Metrics for Item Recommendation",
      "link": "https://research.google/pubs/on-sampled-metrics-for-item-recommendation/",
      "contributions": [
        "Shows that sampled recommendation metrics can differ systematically from full-catalog metrics."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not justify changing the pinned evaluator.",
        "Does not predict whether the proposed modification improves sampled validation HR@10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[4] CL4SRec",
      "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.14395",
      "contributions": [
        "Uses cropping, masking and reordering to construct contrastive sequence views alongside next-item learning.",
        "Establishes a clear precedent limiting claims of originality for random cropping."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Its contrastive-view setting differs from supervised all-position NextItNet training.",
        "Does not isolate context removal from the supervision changes in this proposal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[5] DuoRec",
      "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.05730",
      "contributions": [
        "Motivates avoiding semantic inconsistency from data augmentation through dropout views and same-target positive sequences."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not establish that every prefix crop changes semantics.",
        "Its contrastive method is not implemented in the selected experiment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[6] EC4SRec",
      "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.01347",
      "contributions": [
        "Motivates importance-guided sequence augmentation because random transformations can remove useful information."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not supply validated item-importance estimates for this benchmark.",
        "Importance-guided augmentation would add implementation and diagnostic complexity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[7] RecBole NextItNet implementation",
      "link": "https://recbole.io/docs/v1.1.1/_modules/recbole/model/sequential_recommender/nextitnet.html",
      "contributions": [
        "Provides an explicit example of causal left padding, residual blocks and channel normalization.",
        "Illustrates why receptive-field calculations must count actual convolution dilations."
      ],
      "limitations": [
